environment = "linux/x86_64, the pinned builder image explorer-elixir-builder:v10.2.6 with a postgres:16 sidecar per umbrella application, node 22 and yarn 1 in explorer/frontend, the build volume of this working tree created empty by this run"
outcome = "fail"
evidence = ".logs/wave-gate-3.1.log"
note = "The gate ran once on the merged tip and exited 124: the four per-application backend legs passed in order - block_scout_web 47 tests, ethereum_jsonrpc 25, explorer 113, indexer 46, 0 failures and nothing excluded or skipped in any of them, logs build/explorer-gates/backend-<application>.log - and the frontend dependency leg was still fetching packages when the twenty-minute wrap of the verify_cmd expired, so no leg exhausted its own 1080-second budget, the gate reported no failing leg, and the frontend type check and vitest legs never started, for which no record is written. The whole Elixir dependency tree compiled inside the first backend leg because the build volume of this working tree was created by this run, which is the time the wrap had no room for, so the expiry is read as the cold cost of a first run in this tree rather than as a defect of any task; the run is not repeated here, and task 3.1 keeps the status and evidence it already carries because two of its required tasks, 2.14 and 4.1, are recorded implemented rather than done."

